# The fight commands, with only area_update running, so a fight is the round a command starts. In the temple (3001),
# with Hassan: Smokegod (60, with wiznet's flags and deaths on), Warden (60), Decimus (10, a warrior in no clan),
# Pickpocket (13, a thief in clan rom), Yeoman (5, rom), Clansman (20, rom) and Seer (20, in no clan). A kill or a
# murder makes the attacker wait a round (12 pulses), which the scenario waits out.
# - kill and murder: no one named, no one here, yourself, a mob in a safe room (the altar, 3054), players (is_safe:
#   no clan, theirs), a mob fighting someone outside the group (kill stealing), and a second mob while fighting
# - murder: the victim yells for help, and Pickpocket becomes a KILLER; a charmed duck told to murder does nothing
# - flee: not fighting, and fleeing (each try draws a door), losing 10 experience; Pickpocket, a thief, may sneak
#   away instead
# - surrender: not fighting, and to a fido, which ignores it and attacks
# - Clansman's charmed duck, told to kill Pickpocket, whom Clansman is fighting, stops following (check_killer)
# - sla, and slay: no one, yourself, a player of your trust, a mob and a player
@connect god
Smokegod
smoke123
@return
@return
wiznet on
wiznet flags
wiznet deaths
@connect war
Warden
smoke123
@return
@return
goto 3001
